[{:seon.task/name "a-sync-lock-wait-does-not-poll"
  :seon.task/plan "Found 2026-11-11 by the sweep after Datahike's writer loop (a wait that polled (timeout 0) ran one core for good; fixed in Datahike b59900b2). The one other polling wait on our path: ``konserve.core/wait``, which the ``locked`` macro calls for every synchronous store op that takes a key's lock: (while (not (poll! lock)) (Thread/sleep (rand-int 20))) under the :clj reader branch. It sleeps between polls, so it cannot spin, but it is a clock standing in for a dependency (docs/clocks.md#if-nothing-has-changed-we-do-nothing): a waiter wakes up to 20 ms after the lock is free, and a lock that is never released is waited on for ever with nothing said. Not measured: whether Jolt reads this branch on Seon's paths (the LMDB store may take no konserve lock at all) and how often a wait happens. First: count calls of ``konserve.core/wait`` that find the lock held, over one whole prove. If none, the finding is a wiki line and this task closes; if some, the wait takes from the lock's channel (a blocking take that parks a fiber) and the poll goes."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{}}]
